hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2146","Anba Qutaybah bin Saeed said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God visited God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to his mother’s grave, so he wept and those around him wept, and said: “I asked my Lord for permission to ask forgiveness for her, but He did not I will be given permission, and I asked him for permission to visit her grave, so he gave me permission, so visit the graves, for they remind of death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2147","Anba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Thawr, narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of His father, he said: When Abu Talib was about to die, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon him, and Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi were with him. Umayyah, so he said: Yes, uncle, say there is no god but Allah, a word with which I will argue with you with God. So he said to him: Abu Jahl, and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah: O Abu Talib, do you renounce the religion of Abdul Muttalib? They did not stop talking to him until he said the last thing he spoke to them was: Following the religion of Abdul Muttalib, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will ask for forgiveness.” For you as long as I have not forbidden you.” Then it was revealed: “It is not for the Prophet and those who have believed to ask forgiveness for the polytheists,” and it was revealed: “Indeed, you do not guide whom you love.” But God guides whom He wills (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2148","Abba Ishaq bin Mansour, he said: Abba Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali, he said: I heard a man He asks forgiveness for his parents while they are polytheists, so I said: Do you ask forgiveness for them while they are polytheists? He said: Did Abraham not ask for forgiveness for his father? So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, so it was revealed: And it was not seeking forgiveness. Abraham to his father, except for a promise he made to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2149","Anba Yusuf bin Saeed said: Hajjaj told us, he is the one-eyed man, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika told me that he heard Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah says: I heard Aisha speaking. She said: Shall I not tell you about me and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? We said: Yes, she said: When the night that was with me came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned over, placed his sandals on his feet, and spread He spread his cloak on his bed, and only stayed until he thought that I had fallen asleep. Then he slowly put on his shoes, took his cloak slowly, then opened the door. Slowly, he left, and I put my shield on my head, covered myself, and covered myself with my garment, and I set off in pursuit of him until he came to Al-Baqi’, and he raised his hands. Three times, and he continued for a long time, then he deviated, and I deviated, and he hurried, and I hurried, and he hurried, and I hurried, and he came, and I came, and I outpaced him. So I went in, and it wasn't until I lay down that he went in and said: \What's the matter with you"
"2150","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a recitation of it, and the pronunciation is his, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me On the authority of Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah, on the authority of his mother, that she heard Aisha say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up one night and dressed. His clothes, then he went out. She said: So I ordered my maid Barira to follow him, so I followed him until he came to Al-Baqi’, and he stood at the bottom of it as long as God willed that he should stop. Then he left, and Bareerah overtook him and told me, but I did not mention anything to him until the morning. Then I mentioned that to him, and he said: “I “I was sent to the people of Al-Baqi’ to pray for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2151","Anba Ali bin Hajar told us: Ismail, who is Ibn Jafar, told us: Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr told us, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out every night. At the end of the night, he went to Al-Baqi’, and said: “Peace be upon you, the abode of a believing people, and you and I will meet tomorrow, and we will postpone, and we will, God willing.” We will catch up with you. O God, forgive the people of Baqi’ al-Gharqad.”"
"2152","Abba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, he said: Harami bin Amara told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of His father, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come to the graves, he would say: “Peace be upon you, people of the land, from among the believers and Muslims. And we, God willing, will follow you. You are our successor, and we are your followers. I ask God for well-being for us and for you.”"
"2153","Anba Qutayba bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When Al-Najashi died, the Prophet said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Ask forgiveness for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2154","Anba Abu Dawud, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abd told me. Al-Rahman, and Ibn Al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurairah told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned for them the Negus, the companion of Abyssinia, in The day he died, and he said: “Ask forgiveness for your brother.”"
"2155","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Abd al-Warith bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed those who visit graves and those who place mosques and lamps over them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2156","Narrated by Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Wakee’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For one of you to sit on an ember until his clothes are burned is better than for him to sit on a grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2157","Abba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abd al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib, said: Abba al-Layth, said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hazm, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Abdullah Al-Sulami, on the authority of Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “No You sit on the graves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2158","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse a people who take the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2159","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim Sa’iqa, he said: Abba Abu Salamah Al-Khuza’i, he said: Abba Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse the Jews, they took The graves of their prophets are mosques.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2160","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Shayban, and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Khalid bin Samir, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Khasaiyah, said: I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he passed by the graves of Muslims. He said: “These have preceded much evil.” Then he passed by the graves of the polytheists and said: “These have indeed preceded much good.” So she came to him. He turned around and saw a man walking among the graves in his sandals, so he said: “O owner of the two Sabbaths, throw them away.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2161","Abba Ahmad bin Abi Ubayd Allah Al-Warraq said: Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet of God prayed He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When a servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he will hear the tapping of their sandals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2162","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, and Ibrahim bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Jawzjani, said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Anas bin Malik narrated to us, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a servant is placed in His grave, and his companions turned away from him. He could hear the tapping of their sandals. He said: Two angels would come to him and make him sit down, and they would say to him: What were you saying? About this man? As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of God and His Messenger. Then he is told: Look at your seat in the Fire. God will exchange for it a seat in Paradise.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So he will see them all.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2163","Abba Ahmad bin Abi Ubayd Allah Al-Basri Al-Warraq said: Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When a servant is placed in his grave, and his companions turn away from him, he hears the tapping of their sandals. Two angels sit him down and say: What did you say about this man Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace? As for the believer, he says: I bear witness? He is the servant of God and His Messenger, so it will be said to him: Look at your seat in the Fire. God has given you something better than him.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He, peace and blessings be upon him: “And he will see them.” As for the infidel or hypocrite, it will be said to him: What did you say about this man? He says: I don't know. I was saying what people say. Then he is told: You neither knew nor followed. Then he is struck between his ears and shouts. Then whoever is next to him, other than the heavy ones, will hear it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2164","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Jami’ bin Shaddad told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yassar says: I was sitting with Suleiman bin Surad and Khalid bin Arafat, and they mentioned a man who had died. He died of his stomach, and behold, they They longed to be witnesses of his funeral, so one of them said to the other: Did not the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach, Will he not be tortured in his grave?” The other said: “Yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2165","Abba Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, that Safwan bin Amr He told him, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a man said: O Messenger of God! What is the matter with the believers who are tested in their graves except the martyr? ! He said: “The flash of swords over his head is enough of a temptation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2166","Abba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Aamir bin Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: “ Plague, stomach, drowning, and bloodletting are testimony.” He said: Abu Uthman told us repeatedly, and once he attributed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2167","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: Abba Amr bin Muhammad said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the one for whom the throne moved, and for whom the gates of heaven were opened, and seventy thousand people witnessed him.” The angels. He joined a group of people, then released him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This means Saad bin Muadh. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2168","Abba Ishaq bin Mansour said: Abba Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of al-Bara’, he said: God strengthens those who Believe in the saying that is established regarding the life of this world. He said: “It descended into the torment of the grave.”"
"2169","Abba Muhammad bin Bashar told us: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God establishes those who believe in the firm word regarding the life of this world. He said: It was revealed in The torment of the grave, it will be said to him: Who is your Lord? So he says: My Lord is God, and my Prophet Muhammad. That is His saying. God establishes those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2170","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr reported, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a voice from a grave, and said: “When Did this one die? They said: He died during pre-Islamic times. He was pleased with that, and said: “If you had not buried me, I would have prayed to God to make you feel the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2171","Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Bara’, On the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out after the sun had set, and he heard a voice and said: “Jews are being tortured in their graves.” \"" 2172"""""
"2172","Yahya ibn Durust al-Basri informed us, saying: Abu Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that Abu Salamah narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal)."""""
"2173","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad Al-Misri reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after that seeking refuge from the torment of the grave.”"
"2174","Abba Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, said: Yunus informed me. Ibn Shihab said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Asma’ bint Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and “mentioned the temptation with which a person is tempted in his grave,” so when When he mentioned that, the Muslims became turmoil, which prevented me from understanding the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When their tumult ceased, I I said to a man close to me: May God bless you. What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say at the end of his statement? He said: He said: “It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in the graves, close to the trial of the Antichrist.”"
"2175","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He used to teach them this supplication just as he taught them the surah from the Qur’an. They said: “O God, we seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, and we seek refuge in You from The torment of the grave, and we seek refuge in you from the temptation of the Antichrist, and we seek refuge in you from the temptation of life and death.”"
"2176","Anba Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa told me that Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me, and with me was a Jewish woman, and she was saying: You are being tested in graves. So the Messenger of God was terrified. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “The Jews will be put to trial.” Aisha said: We stayed for several nights, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Is “I felt that it was revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves.” Aisha said: “So I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, later seeking refuge from \the torment of the grave\"""""""
"2177","Abba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: was He seeks refuge from the torment of the grave, and from the temptation of the Antichrist, and he said: “Indeed, you will be tried in your graves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2178","Narrated by Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, a Jewish woman entered upon her. So she asked for something as a gift, and Aisha gave it to her, and she said: May God protect you from the torment of the grave. Aisha said: Then I fell into my soul from the torment of the grave. That is until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and I mentioned that to him, and he said: “They will be tortured in their graves with a torment that you can hear.” \the beasts\"""""""
"2179","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He entered Two elderly women, among the Jews of Medina, came upon me, and they said: The people of the graves are being tortured in their graves, so I denied them, and I was not blessed to believe them. So they went out, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and I said: O Messenger of God, two elderly women among the Jews of Medina said to me: The people of the graves are tortured in their graves. He said: “You are right. They are being tortured with a torment that all animals can hear. I have never seen him pray a prayer without seeking refuge.” from the torment of the grave” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2180","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger passed by God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in one of the walls of Mecca or Medina, and he heard the sound of two people being tortured in their graves, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “They will be punished, but they will not be punished for a major sin.” Then he said: “Yes, one of them was not covering himself from his urine, and the other was walking.” With gossip, then he called for a piece of paper, broke it into two pieces, and placed a piece of it on each of their graves. Then it was said to him: O Messenger of God, why did you do that? This? ! He said: “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry out or until they dry out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2181","Abba Hanad bin Al-Sirri, in his hadith on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) greeted two graves, and he said: “They will be tortured, but they will not be tortured in any grave way. As for one of them, he did not protect himself from his urine, and as for the other... He used to go around gossiping, then he took a damp newspaper and tore it into two halves, then stuck one in each grave. They said: O Messenger of God, why? Did you make this? ! He said: “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not become stiff.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not understand some of Abu Muawiyah’s letters as I wanted to. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2182","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Is not one of you If he dies, his seat will be offered to him in the morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then he will be from the people of Paradise, and if he is one of the people of Hell, He will be among the people of Hell, until God resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2183","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Al-Mu’tamir, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah narrating, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If he dies, his seat will be offered to one of you in the morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Hell, it will be said: This is your seat.” Until God resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"2184","Anba Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, his pronunciation, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you dies, he is presented to his seat in the morning.” And in the evening, if he is from the people of Paradise, then from the people of Paradise, and if he is from the people of Hell, then from the people of Hell, it will be said to him: This is your seat. Until God resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2185","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b that he informed him: His father Ka’b bin Malik He was speaking on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The breath of a believer is merely a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until God returns him to his body on the day He will be resurrected.”"
"2186","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Yahya told us: He is Ibn Sa`id. He said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: We were with Omar between Mecca and Medina, and he started telling us about the people of Badr, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace To show us their struggle the day before, that is, this is the death of so-and-so, God willing, tomorrow. Omar said: By the One who sent him with the truth, they had not made a mistake. So they were placed in a well, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them and called: “O so-and-so son of so-and-so, oh so-and-so son of so-and-so, have you found what he promised you?” Is your Lord truly true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” Omar said: Am I speaking to bodies that have no souls in them? He said: “You are not better at listening to what I say than they are.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2187","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr Al-Marwazi, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Muslims heard, at night in the well of Badr, He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing and calling: “O Abu Jahl bin Hisham, O Shayba bin Rabi’ah, O Utba bin Rabi’ah, O Umayyah bin Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of God, are you calling a people who have They dried out? ! He said: “You are not better at listening to what I say than they are, but they are not able to answer.”"
"2188","Abba Muhammad bin Adam said: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood at the heart of Badr, and he said: “Have you found what your Lord promised to be true?” And he said: “They will now hear what I say.” So that was mentioned to Aisha, and she said: Is it Ibn Umar? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “They now know that what I was telling them is the truth. Then I read... His saying: You do not hear the dead, until you read the verse (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2189","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, and Mughirah, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “All the sons of Adam.” And in the hadith of Mughirah: “Every son of Adam eats it, meaning dirt, except the tailbone, from which he was created and in which he is built.”"
"2190","Anba Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, Blessed and Most High, said: “The son of Adam has lied to me and it was not appropriate for him to do so.” He denies Me, and the son of Adam insulted Me, and he should not have insulted Me. As for his denial of Me, he said: I will not repeat it as I started it. The last of creation is not more dear to me than its first, and as for his cursing of me, he said: God has begotten a son, and I am God the One, God the Eternal, I have not given birth. “I was not born, and there was no one equal to me.”"
"2191","Anba Kathir bin Ubaid said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A servant was extravagant with himself, and when death approached him, he said to his family: If I died, so burn me, then crush me, then throw me in the wind in the sea. By God, if God has power over me, He will torture me with a torment that no one else has ever tormented. Of His creation. He said: So his family did that. God said to everyone who took something from him: Give back what you took. And lo, he will stand. God said. Blessed and Most High: What made you do what you did? He said: Your fear, so God forgave him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2192","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “There was a man before you who had bad thoughts about his work, and when death approached him,” he said to his family: “Then I will die.” So they burned me, then ground me, then threw me into the sea, for God has power over me. He has not forgiven me. He said: So God commanded the angels, Then his soul touched him, and he said to him: What made you do what you did? He said: O Lord, I only did it out of fear of You, so God forgave him."
"2193","I am Qutayba bin Saeed. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: “Indeed, you will meet God barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.”"
"2194","Abba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Al-Nu’man told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the Day of Resurrection, people will be gathered naked and barefoot. The first of the creation will be Abraham, then He recited: “We will return the first creation” as a promise upon us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2195","Anba Amr bin Othman bin Saeed bin Kathir said: Baqiya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the Day of Resurrection, people will be raised barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” So Aisha said: Oh Messenger of God, so what about private parts? ! He said: Every one of them will have a matter on that day that will enrich him."
"2196","Anba Amr bin Ali told me: Yahya told us, he said: Abu Yunus al-Qushayri told us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will be gathered barefoot and naked.” I said: Should the men and women look at each other? ! He said: “The matter is too severe for them to care about that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2197","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Abu Hisham, who is Al-Mughirah bin Salamah, told us: Thana Wahib is Ibn Khalid. Abu Bakr, who said: Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people will be gathered on the day The Resurrection will be in three ways: two monks willing, two upon a camel, three upon a camel, four upon a camel, and ten upon a camel, and you will be gathered together. The Fire will remain with them. It will abide with them wherever they stayed, stay with them wherever they stayed, stay with them wherever they stayed, and stay with them wherever they stayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2198","Anba Amr bin Ali said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, he said: Abu Tufayl told us, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Usayd, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: The Truthful, the Trustworthy, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “The people will be gathered in three groups: riding, eating, and cupping, and a group of The angels will drag them on their faces and the fire will surround them, and they will often be touched and run. God will cast the calamity on the back, but it will not remain. “For a man to have a great garden, he gives it in the same way that he is not able to handle it.”"
"2199","Anba Mahmoud bin Ghaylan said: Waki’, Wahb, who is Ibn Jarir bin, and Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to deliver the sermon, and he said: “O People, you will be gathered together before God naked.” Abu Dawud said: “barefoot and barefoot,” and Waki’ and Wahb said: “barefoot and naked,” as we started at the beginning. A creation that We will restore. He said: “The first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Abraham, and he will come.” Abu Dawud said: “He will come.” Wahb said, Waki’: “Men from my nation will be brought, and they will be taken to the north. Then I will say: Lord of my companions,” and it will be said: You do not know what they did after you. So I say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them, but when you caused me to die, you were the watcher over them and you are over everything. Witness {117} If You punish them, then they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise. {118} Until the end of the verse, it is said: Indeed These people are still backsliding. Abu Dawud said: “They have been backsliding since you separated from them.”"
"2200","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar al-Mawsili informed me, on the authority of al-Mu’affa, on the authority of Zakaria ibn Ishaq al-Makki, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah bin Saifi, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Muadh bin Jabal when he sent him: To Yemen: “You are coming to a people, People of the Book, so when you come to them, call them to bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad Messenger of God, if they obey that, then tell them that God has enjoined upon them five prayers in a day and a night, if that means they obeyed. So, tell them that God has imposed on them zakat to be taken from their rich and given to their poor, so if they obey you. Thus, fear the call of the oppressed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2201","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Mu`tamar told us, saying: I heard Bahz ibn Hakim telling, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I said: O Prophet of God, I did not come to you until I had sworn by more than their number, on the fingers of his hands, that I would not come to you nor follow your religion, and that I was a woman who did not I understand nothing except what God and His Messenger have taught me, and I ask you in the face of God: Why has your Lord sent you to us? He said: “By Islam.” I said: What are the signs of Islam? He said: “That you say: I have surrendered my face to God and renounced myself, and perform prayer and pay zakat,” and on the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Bukayr, on the authority of Shibl bin Abbad, on the authority of Abu Qaza Suwayd bin Hujayr, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2202","Issa bin Musawar reported, saying: Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Sabour told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of his brother, who is Zayd bin Salam, that He told him, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Salam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, that Abu Malik al-Ash’ari told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And peace be upon him, he said: “Performing ablution thoroughly is half of faith, and praise be to God fills the scale, and glorification and glorification fill the heavens and the earth, and prayer “Light, zakat is proof, patience is illumination, and the Qur’an is proof for you or against you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2203","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, who said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Naim Al-Mujmar, Abu Abdullah, said: Suhaib told me that he heard from Abu Hurairah, and from Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, three times, then a man among us began to cry, not knowing what he swore about, then he raised his head in He brought good news to us, and it was dearer to us than red camels, then he said: “There is no servant who prays the five daily prayers, fasts Ramadan, and goes out... Zakat, and he avoids the seven calamities except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him, and it will be said to him: Enter in peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2204","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd told me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever spends two pairs of He will be called from the gates of Paradise, O servant of God, this is good, and Paradise has gates, so whoever is among the people of prayer will be invited. For the sake of prayer, and whoever was among the people of jihad will be called for the sake of jihad, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called for the sake of charity, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called for the sake of charity. The people of fasting were called from the gate of Ar-Rayyan.” Abu Bakr said: Is it necessary for the one who is called from those gates? Will he be called from all of them? Anyone, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes, and I hope that you are one of them, meaning Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq.”"
"2205","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Ma’ar bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaaba. When he saw me approaching, he said: “They are the losers, by the Lord of the Kaaba.” So I said: What do I have to do with me? I went down about something. I said: Who are they? May my father and mother be sacrificed for you? He said: “Those who have the most wealth, except for those who say: Thus and thus.” So he looked between his hands, on his right, and on his left, then he said: “By the One who is my soul.” By his hand, no man dies and leaves behind camels or cows without paying their zakat, but they will come on the Day of Resurrection, the greatest and fattest they have ever been, and the fattest they have ever set foot on. with their socks and gore him with their horns, and whenever the last of them goes out, the first of them is returned to him until he judges among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2206","Narrated by Mujahid bin Musa, who said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no man who has money who does not pay what is due from him, but He will put a collar around his neck, a brave man who knocks, and he will flee from him.” And he follows it.” Then he read its confirmation from the Book of God: And let not those who are stingy with what God has given them of His bounty think that it is better for them. Rather, it is evil for them. They will contain what they were stingy with.”"
"2207","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu Umar. Al-Ghadani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Any man who owns camels does not give them their right to I helped her and her messengers.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what did I help her and her messengers? He said: “In its hardship and its ease, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as the most nutritious, fattest, and worst of all it was. So she treads on him with her hoofs, and when she passes the last of them, the first of them is returned to him on a day whose equivalent is fifty thousand years, until it is spent among the people. So he will see his way, and any man who owns cows does not give them their right to help them and messengers, they will come on the Day of Resurrection as fodder. Whatever it is, and the fattest and ugliest, it will be spread out on a rumbling bottom, and every horned animal will gore it with its horn, and every hoofed animal will trample it. With her unmarried woman, when her last one passed him, her children were given back to him on a day the equivalent of fifty thousand years, until it was judged among the people and he would see His way, and any man who owns sheep does not give them their rights in helping them and messengers, they will come on the Day of Resurrection as the fodder of any sheep. It was the thickest, the fattest, and the ugliest, then a gushing bottom would be laid out for it, and every living creature would trample it with its hoof, and every living creature would gore it. A horn for its horn, in which there is neither a dent nor a bite. If the last of it exceeds it, the first of it is returned to him. On a day the amount of it was fifty thousand. a year until it is decided among the people and he sees his way.”"
"2208","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin told me Utbah bin Masoud, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and Abu Bakr was appointed as his successor after him, and he disbelieved. Whoever among the Arabs disbelieves, Omar said to Abu Bakr: How do you fight people? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. Whoever says: There is no god but God will be protected from me.” His wealth and his soul except according to his right, and his reckoning is with God.” Abu Bakr said: “By God, I will fight whoever differentiates between prayer and zakat, for zakat is the right of money.” By God, if they had withheld from me a camel that they were giving to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have fought them for withholding it. Omar said: By God, it is nothing but If I saw God open Abu Bakr’s heart to fight, then I would know that it is the truth."
"2209","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Bahz bin Hakim told us, he said: my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “In every free-moving camel, in every forty bint Labun, no camels are separated from their reckoning, whoever gives them to a lessor.” He will have its reward, and whoever refuses, we will take it and split his camel in halves, one of the gifts of our Lord, none of which is lawful for the family of Muhammad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2210","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Amr bin Yahya told me. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan, Shu’bah, and Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no charity for anything less than five wasqs, nor for “Below five dawds is a zakat, and there is no zakat on anything less than five uwqs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2211","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no zakat for less than five dawd, nor for what is less than five uwaqs.” “Silver is a charity, and nothing less than five wasqs is a charity.”"
"2212","Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak said: Abu Kamil al-Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: I took this book from Thumamah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Bakr wrote for them:\n\n\These are the obligatory acts of charity (Sadaqah) that the Messenger of Allah"
"2213","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zanad told me, from what Abdul Rahman told him Al-Araj, from what he mentioned, is that he heard Abu Hurairah speaking about it. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Camels come to their Lord for the best of things.” If her right was not given to her, she would tread on it with her cloaks, and the sheep would come to their master as well as they were if his right was not given to her. So they trample him with their hooves and gore him with their horns, and it is their right to be milked on water. Will none of you bring a camel on the Day of Resurrection? He carries it on his neck, with a bow, and says: O Muhammad, so I say: I do not own anything for you, as I have conveyed it. None of you will come to me on the Day of Resurrection. With a sheep that he carries on his neck, he will be taunted, and he will say: O Muhammad, so I will say: I do not own anything for you, as I have attained it, and it will be someone’s treasure on the Day of Judgment. Resurrection is a brave one who knocks. His friend flees from him and seeks him. I am your treasure. He will not continue with it until his finger touches it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2214","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Mu`tamar told us, saying: I heard Bahz ibn Hakim, speaking on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: In every free-running camel out of every forty there is a daughter of Labun. Whoever gives it to a lessor will have its reward, and whoever withholds it - we will take it and divide his camels, one of the punishments of our Lord, none of which is permissible for the family of Muhammad. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2215","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Favorable narration, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of a brother, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Muadh, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Yemen, and ordered him to take from every dreamer a dinar or a large amount of money, And of the cows: thirty tabi’ah or tabi’ah, and forty mature cows.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2216","Ahmad ibn Sulaiman al-Rahwi reported, saying: Ya`la ibn Ubaid told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: Muadh said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen, and he ordered me to take a second cow from every forty, and from every Thirty tabi'a, and from every dreamer a dinar or his equivalent of a reward.\"" 2217"""""
"2217","Ahmad ibn Harb informed us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Mu'adh, who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent him to Yemen, he commanded him to take from every thirty head of cattle a tabi' or tabi'ah (a yearling male or female), and from every forty a musinnah (a two-year-old female), and from every halim (adult/pubescent person) a dinar or its equivalent in ma'afir (Yemeni cloth)."""""
"2218","Muhammad ibn Mansour narrated, he said: Ya’qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman Al-Amash narrated to me, on the authority of my father Wael bin Salamah, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me when he sent me to Yemen not to take from cows.” Nothing until it reaches thirty, then when it reaches thirty then it has a calf attached to it, a stem or stem until it reaches forty, then when it reaches forty Therein is an old cow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2219","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala al-Kufi reported, saying: Muhammad bin Fudayl reported, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no owner of camels, cows, or sheep who does not pay their rights except as an endowment.” On the Day of Resurrection, it will have a roaring bottom that the hoofed creatures will trample with their hooves, and the horned creatures will gore with their horns. There will be no crowds therein that day. Not even a broken horn.” I said: O Messenger of God, and what is the fulfillment of her rights? He said: “Leading her stallion, lending her bucket, and carrying a load for her in the way of God. There is no owner of wealth who does not pay what is due to him but he imagines a day for him.” Resurrection is a brave man who knocks down. His companion flees from him and he follows him, saying to him: This is your treasure, which you were stingy with. So if he sees that He must have put his hand into its mouth and started gnawing on it as a stallion gnaws.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2220","'Ubayd Allah ibn Fadalah informed me, he said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man reported to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Anas ibn Malik, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Bakr wrote for him:\n\n\These are the obligatory acts of charity (Sadaqah) that the Messenger of Allah"
"2221","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no owner of camels, cows, or sheep who does not pay their zakat but that on the Day of Resurrection a greater one will come.” She used to gore him with her horns and trample him with her socks. Whenever the last of them ran out, the first of them would return to him until he was judged among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2222","Hannad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Maysara Abu Salih, on the authority of Suwayd bin Alqamah, who said: A trustworthy ass. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to him and sat next to him, and I heard him say: “In my covenant, we shall not take anything from a breastfed infant, nor combine Divided, and we do not differentiate between two groups.” Then a man came to him with a large she-camel and said: Take it, but he refused. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2223","Harun bin Zaid bin Yazid reported, he said: My father told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael Ibn Hajar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a courier, and he brought a man, and he brought him a deserted detachment, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “ “We have sent a verifier of God and His Messenger, and so-and-so gave him a spoiled camel. O God, do not bless him or his camels.” Then the news reached that man, so he came. With a she-camel, so he mentioned Hassan, and said: I repent to God and to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Oh God, bless On him and on his camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2224","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, Amr bin Murrah said: he told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa said: Whenever people came to him with their charity, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, bless the family of so-and-so.” So my father came to him with charity, and he said: “O God, bless the family of my father, Awfa.”"
"2225","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, and the wording is his, they said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Hilal said: Jarir said: Some Bedouins came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Messenger of God, some Bedouins are coming to us. Those who believe you are treated unjustly. He said: “Satisfy your believers.” They said: And if he is unjust? He said: “Satisfy your believers.” Jarir said: Not a believer has come from me since I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that he was satisfied. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2226","Ziyad bin Ayyub reported, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Dawud reported, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Jarir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If the ratifier comes to you, let him leave it satisfied with you.”"
"2227","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Makhrami reported, saying: Waki` told us, saying: Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim bin Thafna, Ibn Alqamah enlisted the help of my father to do divination for his people, and ordered him to believe them, “So my father sent me with a group of them.” To give him their zakat, so I went out until I came to an old sheikh called Saar, and I said: My father sent me to you so that you could pay the zakat on your sheep. He said “My brother’s son. What direction do you take?” I said: “You choose until we are as wide as the udders of sheep.” He said: “My brother’s son. I tell you that I was there.” One of these areas was during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among my sheep. Then two men came to me on a camel and said: We are the Messenger of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace, so that you may pay the zakat on your sheep. He said: I said: What do I have to do with it? They said: A sheep, so I go to a sheep whose place I know. It was full, clean and fat, so I brought it out to them, and they said: This is the intercessor, and the intercessor is the one who is the one who prevents, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us. And granted that We should appoint an intercessor. He said: So I went to Anak Ma’atat and the one who had not given birth to a child and the time had come for her to give birth, so I took her out. To them, and they said: We gave it to you, so I handed it to them, and they carried it with them on their camels and then set off. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know anyone. Waki' continued his saying: Muslim bin Thafna, and others said: Muslim bin Shu'bah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2228","Imran bin Bakkar al-Homsi told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu al-Zannad told me, from what he told him Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from what he mentioned, is that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating: Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the giving of charity. It was said: Ibn Jamil, Khalid ibn al-Walid, and Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib forbade it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ibn Beautiful, except that he was poor, so God enriched him. As for Khaled, you are unjust to Khaled, who retained his armor and his armor in the path of God. Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, the uncle of the Messenger of God, so it is a charity on him, and the same is for it.”"
"2229","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah reported, saying: My father told me, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Moses, he said: Abu al-Zinad told me, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered “to give alms equal to one in equal measure.”"
"2230","Amr bin Mansour and Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, saying: Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, on the authority of Othman bin Abdullah bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hilal Al-Thaqafi, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I almost I will kill your enemy for a shepherd or a sheep in charity. He said: “If it had not been given to the poor of the immigrants, I would not have taken it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2231","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: We are Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not have to do with his slave.” “And his horse is not a charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2232","I am Muhammad bin Mansour. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Arak bin Malik On the authority of Abu Hurairah, referring it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A Muslim does not owe any zakat on his slave or his horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2233","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Mahrez bin Al-Waddah reported, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no zakat due on the Muslim man on His servant, nor his horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2234","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Khathim, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “A person does not have to pay any zakat on his horse or his property.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2235","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading of it and its pronunciation, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, He said: Abdullah bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “A Muslim does not have to pay any zakat on his slave or his horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2236","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Khathim bin Arak bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “A Muslim is not obligated to pay any zakat on his servant or on his horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2237","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, he said: Yaqoub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya bin told me. Hibban, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’ah, and they were trustworthy, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara bin Abi Hussein, And Abbad bin Tamim, and they were trustworthy, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Not in anything less than “Five awqa of paper is zakat, and there is no zakat on less than five camels, and there is no zakat on less than five wasqs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2238","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, on the authority of Hammad, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no zakat on what is less than five uwqs, nor on what is less than five dawds, nor on what “Below five wasqs is charity.”"
"2239","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, on the authority of Malik, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin told me. Abu Sa`sa`ah al-Mazni, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Not among less than five “An one-ounce of dates is zakat, and there is no zakat on anything less than five ounces of dates, and there is no zakat on anything less than five camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2240","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa`sa'ah, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, and Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “There is no charity for less than five wasqs of dates, nor for less than five wasqs of paper, nor for less than five camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2241","Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have pardoned horses and slaves, so pay the zakat on your property, five for every two hundred.”"
"2242","Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damrah, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have pardoned horses and slaves, and there is no zakat on anything less than two hundred.”"
"2243","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that A woman from the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with her daughter. In her daughter’s hand were two thick golden holders. He said: “Do you pay the zakat on this?” She said: No. He said: “Would God please you for two bracelets of fire on the Day of Resurrection with them?” He said: So she took them off. So she gave them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: They are God and His Messenger. Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu`tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Husayn bin Dhakwan, the visual teacher, who is trustworthy, saying: Amr bin Shuaib narrated to me, saying: She came A woman and her daughter were with her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in her daughter’s hand were two muscats, something like mursal, Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: Khaled bin Al-Harith is more proven to us than Al-Mu’tamir, and the hadith of Al-Mu’tamir is better, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2244","Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj told us, he said: Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi told us Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who does not pay the zakat on his wealth will imagine To him will be his wealth on the Day of Resurrection. He is brave and has two raisins for him.” He said: “He will cling to him or surround him.” He said: He will say: “I am your treasure. \Your treasure\"""""""
"2245","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Hassan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar al-Madani told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever God Almighty and Majestic gives wealth and does not pay it back.” His zakat. His wealth will be represented to him on the Day of Resurrection as a brave man. He will be given two raisins. He will take them with two of them on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say: I am yours. I am your treasure. Then he recited this verse: “And let not those who are miserly think.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah proved We have from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, and the narration of Abd al-Rahman is more similar to the truth in our view, and God knows best, even if it is Abdul Rahman is not that strong in hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2246","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Not in anything less than “Five wasqs of grains and dates are charity.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ismail. I do not know of anyone who followed him on his statement: “From grain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2247","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Amr bin Yahya told me. Ibn Amara, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “It is not permissible to pay zakat on wheat and dates until It is five auqs, and it is not permissible to pay zakat on paper until it reaches five auqs, and it is not permissible to pay zakat on camels until it reaches five camels.”"
"2248","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is neither grain nor dates.” “Zakat is not given until it reaches five awqs, nor is it zakat for less than five auq, nor is it zakat for what is less than five awqs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2249","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Waki’ told us, saying: Idris Al-Awdi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no charity for anything less than five wasaqs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2250","Ahmad bin Abdah reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no charity on what is less than five uqs, nor on what is less than five uqs. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2251","Harun bin Saeed reported, he said: Ibn Wahb reported, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While the sky and the rivers and springs were irrigated, or Baal was the tithe, and what was irrigated by groves or dripping water, half “The tithe,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Nafi’ narrated it, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, his saying, and Salim and Nafi’ differed over Ibn Umar in three Hadiths: This is one of them. The second: “Whoever sells a slave while he owns it.” He said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Nafi’ said: On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, his statement, and Salim said on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Fire comes out from before Yemen,” and Nafi’ said, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Salem is more honorable and noble than Nafi’. The three hadiths of Nafi’ are more deserving of the truth, and God grant us success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2252","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr, Ahmad ibn Amr, and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported to me, and it was read to him while I was listening. On the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith told us that Abu al-Zubayr told him that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “With what was irrigated by the sky, the rivers, and the clouds, a tenth, and with what was irrigated by the tongue, half a tenth,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith except Amr bin Al-Harith. And Ibn Jurayj, narrated it on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, his saying, and the hadith of Ibn Jurayj is more deserving of authenticity according to us, even if Amr ibn Al-Harith is better memorized than him, and by God, grant us success. Abdul Rahman said: Amr bin Al-Harith is one of the memorizers. Malik narrated on his authority"
"2253","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Muadh, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me May God bless him and grant him peace, to Yemen, and he commanded me to take a tenth of what the sky watered, and half a tenth of what was irrigated by the peddles,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: This chain of narration is also not that strong, because Abu Bakr bin Ayyash and Asim are not memorizers."
"2254","Muhammad ibn Bashhar informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa`id and Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed us, saying: Shu`bah informed us, saying: I heard Habib ibn Abdul Rahman, narrating on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Masoud bin Dinar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, he said: He came to us while we were in the market, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you have made a bid, take and leave a third. If you do not take or leave a third, Shu’bah doubts, then leave.” \Quarter\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2255","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Sakin reported a reading of it, and I am listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Abd al-Jalil narrated to me. Bin Humayd Al-Yahsbi, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, saying: Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated to me, in the verse in which God said: And “Temple the evil things from which you spend.” He said: “He is the Ja’rūr, and the color of Hubayq.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them from being taken as part of charity."
"2256","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya, who is the son of Sa’id al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Ja’far, he said: Saleh bin Abi told me Oraib, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah al-Khudharami, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja’i, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out with a staff in his hand. A man commented on the quotation of Hashf, and he began to challenge that quotation, and he said: “If the Lord had wanted this charity, he would have given something better than this. “The Lord of this charity will eat away the gossip on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"2257","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the snapshot, and he said: “It was not on the way of a coming person or in a populated town, so he recognized it as a year.” If its owner comes, otherwise it is yours, and as long as it is not on a well-traveled road, nor in a populated town, then it is in it and in the five pillars.”"
"2258","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: And Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said “The blind woman’s wound is mighty, and the well is mighty, and the mine is mighty, and in the five ores,” Yunus ibn Abd al-A’la reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed, and Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: the same. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2259","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The wound of the blind is mighty, the well is mighty, the mineral is mighty, and the five ores are mighty.”"
"2260","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour and Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The well is mighty, and the oppressed are mighty, and the miner is mighty, and in the ore \the fifth\"""""""
"2261","Al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani told me, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Shuaib informed me, Musa ibn Ayan said, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Hilal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with tens of his palm trees. And he asked him to protect for him a valley called Salba. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, protected that valley for him. When Omar bin Al-Khattab Sufyan bin Wahb wrote to Omar bin Al-Khattab asking him, so Omar wrote: If he performs to you what he performed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May peace be upon him and grant him peace from a tenth of his palm trees, so protect the spoils of that for him. Otherwise, they are merely rainflies that may be eaten by whomever they wish.”"
"2262","Imran bin Musa Al-Basri reported, on the authority of Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed Al-Basri, who said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed the Ramadan zakat on the free man, male and female, a saa’ of dates or a saa’ of barley. So the people gave it half a saa’ of wheat.”"
"2263","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed He gave the zakat al-fitr to the male and female, the free man and the slave: a saa’ of dates or a saa’ of barley. He said: So the people amounted to half a saa’ of barley. Righteousness"
"2264","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it obligatory Ramadan zakat is due on every young and old, free and slave, male and female, a saa’ of dates or a saa’ of barley.”"
"2265","Muhammad bin Salamah reported to Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry, and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “obligated zakat al-fitr from Ramadan The people are entitled to a saa of dates or a saa of barley, and to every Muslim free man or slave, male or female. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2266","Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, he said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed Zakat al-Fitr as one Saa’ of dates, or one Saa’ of barley on the free man and the slave. And male and female, and young and old among the Muslims, and he commanded that it be performed before the people go out to pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2267","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Issa, who is Ibn Yunus, narrated, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed Zakat al-Fitr on young and old, male and female, free and slave, a saa’ of dates or a saa' of barley\"" 2268"""""
"2268","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Basri informed us, saying: Yazid (ibn Zuray') narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from 'Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: ""We used to fast 'Ashura' and pay Zakat al-Fitr. When Ramadan was revealed and Zakat was revealed, we were not commanded to do it nor forbidden from it, and we used to do it."""""
"2269","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, On the authority of Abu Ammar Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to give zakat al-fitr before it descends.” Zakat, and when the zakat came down, he did not order us or forbid us, but we did it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Ammar, whose name is Gharib bin Humayd, and Amr bin Shurahbil, nicknamed Abu Maysara. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2270","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, and he is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Praiseworthy told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ibn Abbas said, and he is The Emir of Basra at the end of the month: “Give the zakat for your fasting.” The people looked at each other and said: “Who is here from the people of Medina? Arise and teach your brothers, for they do not know that this zakat was imposed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on every male. And the female free and owned: a saa’ of barley or dates or half a saa’ of wheat.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan did not hear from Ibn Abbas was disagreed with by Hisham on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2271","Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, on the authority of Mukhlid, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was mentioned regarding zakat al-fitr, He said: “A saa of wheat, or a saa of dates, or a saa of barley, or a saa of wheat.”"
"2272","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Raja, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas, delivering a sermon on your pulpit. Meaning the pulpit of Basra, he says: “Zakat al-Fitr is a saa’ of food.”"
"2273","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb informed me, saying: Mahrez bin Al-Wadah informed me, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Dhabab, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah bin Abi Sarh, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed “The zakat of al-Fitr is a saa’ of barley, or a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of acorn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2274","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, trustworthy, saying: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: “We used to pay Zakat al-Fitr when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had among us a saa’ of food, or “A saa’ of barley, or a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of raisins, or a saa’ of acorns.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2275","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: “We used to go out Zakat al-Fitr, since the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give us a saa’ of food, or a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley, or a saa’ of It remained like that until Muawiyah came from the Levant, and it was about what the people learned about it that he said: I do not see a woman from the city of Samarat al-Sham that is not equivalent to a saa’. From this, he said: So the people took to that."
"2276","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, he said: I heard Iyad bin Abdullah tell, about Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “We did not give out during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anything except a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley, or a saa’ of barley. Of raisins, or a saa of flour, or a saa of aqat, or a saa of salt.” Then Sufyan had doubts, so he said flour or salt. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know anyone who said this hadith accurately except Ibn Uyaynah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know anyone who said this hadith accurately. This hadith: “accurate” other than Ibn Uyaynah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2277","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Yazid reported, he said: Humaid reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Ibn Abbas delivered a sermon in Basra, and he said “Pay the zakat for your fasting.” Then he made the people look at each other and said: “Who is here from the people of Medina? Go to your brothers.” So teach them, for they do not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed Zakat al-Fitr on the young and the old, the free and the slave. And for males and females, half a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of dates or barley.” Al-Hasan said: Then Ali said: “But if God expands upon you, then expand. Give a saa’ of wheat or something else.”"
"2278","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “People used to give as zakat al-fitr during the era of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a saa’ of barley, or dates, or salt. \or raisins\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2279","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told us, he said: Iyad told us, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: “We used to go out... During the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a saa’ of barley, dates, raisins, or acorns, and this did not stop until it was during the reign of Muawiyah. He said: I do not see a woman from Samarra al-Sham that is equivalent to a saa’ of barley."
"2280","Issa bin Hammad Ibn Zaghbah Al-Masry reported, saying: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Uthman. That Iyad bin Abdullah bin Saad narrated to him, that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “We used to go out during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he delivered a saa of dates, or a saa of barley, or a saa of aqt, we will not produce anything else.”"
"2281","Amr ibn Zurarah al-Naysaburi narrated, he said: Al-Qasim, who is Ibn Malik, narrated on the authority of al-Ja’id, he said: I heard al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, He says: “A saa’ during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one mudd and a third of your mudd today, and it has been increased.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated to me by Ziyad bin Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Qasim"
"2282","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahwi reported, saying: Abu Nu’aym told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan Al-Makki, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A measure is the measure of the people of Medina, and the weight is the weight of the people of Mecca.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2283","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us. And Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Al-Fudayl told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the zakat al-fitr to be paid before the people go out to pray.” Ibn Bazi’ said in his hadith: With zakat al-fitr, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is Fudayl ibn Sulaiman. Yahya ibn Ma’in used to weaken him, and Ali ibn al-Madini used to talk about him, and the saying In our view, Yahya is more deserving of what is correct, because we found in Fudayl ibn Sulaiman some reprehensible hadiths, and by God, we grant success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2284","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami informed us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Yahya Bin Abdullah bin Saifi, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Muadh bin Jabal to Yemen, and he said “Indeed, you will come to a people who are People of the Book, so call them to testimony that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God. If they obey you, then teach them.” God has made it obligatory upon them to give charity from their wealth, taken from the rich among them and given to the poor among them. If they obey you for that, beware of you. And their generous wealth, and beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no veil between it and God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2285","Imran bin Bakkar al-Homsi told us, he said: Ali bin Abbas told us, he said: Shuaib, who is the son of Abi Hamza, told us, he said: Abu Hamza told me The trigger is from what was narrated by Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from what he mentioned that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “A man said: Should I give charity to you?” So he went out with his charity and put it in the hands of a thief. They started talking about giving charity to a thief, so he said: Oh God, praise be to You for a thief who gave us charity. He went out with his charity and put it in the hands of an adulteress. They started talking: Give charity. Tonight, he committed an adulteress, so he said: O God, praise be to You for an adulteress. Let me give charity. So he went out with his charity and put it in the hands of a rich man. So they started talking about giving alms to a rich man. He said: O God, praise be to You for an adulteress, a thief, and a rich man. Then he came and was told: Did I not give you alms? It was accepted. As for the adulteress, perhaps she can abstain from her adultery through him, and perhaps the thief can abstain from his theft through him, and perhaps the rich man will abstain from his theft through him. He considers and spends from what God has given him.”"
"2286","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Basri narrated to Al-Dhara’, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us. And Anba Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Shu’bah told us, and the wording is Bishr, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from \Ghouls\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2287","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurairah, saying The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No one gives in charity any good thing, and God does not accept anything but good things, unless the Most Gracious takes it with His right hand.” And if it is a date, then let it be raised in the palm of the Most Gracious until it is greater than a mountain, just as one of you raises his foal or its offspring.”"
"2288","Abd al-Wahhab al-Warraq ibn al-Hakam al-Ruqi reported on the authority of Hajjaj, who is the son of Muhammad. Ibn Jurayj said: Uthman ibn Abi Suleiman informed me. On the authority of Ali Al-Azdi, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habashi Al-Khathami, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: What are the deeds? Better? He said: “Faith in which there is no doubt, jihad in which there is no deceit, and an approved Hajj.” It was said: Which prayer is best? He said: “Length of Qunoot.” It was said: Which charity is better? He said: “The effort of al-Muql.” It was said: Which migration is best? He said: “Whoever abandons what God has forbidden to him.” It was said: Which jihad is better? He said: “He who fights against the polytheists with his wealth and his life.” It was said: Which killing is most honorable? He said: “Whose blood is spilled and whose horse is maimed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2289","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, and Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A hundred thousand dirhams came before a dirham.” They said: How? He said: “A man had two dirhams, so he gave one of them in charity, and a man went to show his money and took one hundred thousand dirhams from him and gave it in charity.”"
"2290","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed narrated, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One hundred thousand dirhams preceded one dirham.” They said: O Messenger of God, and how? He said: “A man had two dirhams, so he took one of them and gave it in charity. And a man had a lot of money, so he took one hundred thousand from his wealth and gave it in charity.” \with it\"""""""
"2291","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Hussein, who is Ibn Waqid Al-Maruzi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of his brother On the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to command us to give charity, but none of us found anything to give in charity until he set out.” To the market, and he carries it on his back and brings it with the tide, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gives it to him. Indeed, today I know a man who has One hundred thousand, he did not have a dirham at that time.”"
"2292","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari reported, saying: Ghandar reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Masoud, He said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to give charity, Abu Aqeel gave half a saa’ in charity, and a person brought something more than him. Then the hypocrites said: God is free from this man’s charity, and this other man did nothing but hypocrisy. So those who touch the obedient believers were revealed. In charity and those who do not find anything but their best.”"
"2293","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Saeed and Urwa told me, they heard Hakim bin Hazam, He says: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, then I asked him, and he gave me, then I asked him, and he gave me, then he said: “Indeed This money is green and sweet, so whoever takes it with good will will be blessed for it, and whoever takes it with good will will not be blessed for it. He was like someone who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"
"2294","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa Al-Maruzi Al-Shaybani reported, saying: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Ziyad. Ibn Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jami’ Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Tariq Al-Muharbi, who said: We approached Medina, and behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He is standing on the pulpit addressing the people, and he says: “The hand of the Giver is on high, and begin with those you support: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother. Then the closest to you, the closest to you,” is brief"
"2295","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he He mentions charity and abstaining from begging: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the upper hand spends, and the lower hand begs.” \"" 2296"""""
"2296","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Bakr (ibn Mudad) narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: ""The best charity is that which is given out of surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those whom you support."" Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: ""This 'Ajlan is the father of Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, and Bukayr narrated from him, and 'Ajlan the mawla of al-Mushma'il, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from him; both of them narrate from Abu Hurayrah."""""
"2297","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym reported, saying: Hibban told us, saying: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no charity for the back of wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. “And start with those you support.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2298","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa’id told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give it in charity.” A man said: O Messenger of God, I have a dinar. He said: “Give it to yourself.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it to your wife.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it to your son.” He said: I have another. He said: Give it to your servant in charity.” He said: “I have another.” He said: “You will see it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2299","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Iyadh, who is the son of Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that a man entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering the sermon, and he said: “Pray two rak’ahs,” then he came The second Friday, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering the sermon, and he said: “Pray two rak’ahs,” then the third Friday came, and he, peace be upon him, said: “Pray Two rak'ahs.\ Then he said: \""Give in charity.\"" They gave in charity"
"2300","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ubaid, who said: I heard Umayr, the servant of Abi al-Lahm, saying: He commanded me My master wanted me to offer him some meat. A poor man came and I fed him some of it. My master learned of that and struck me. I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so he called him and said: “Why did you hit him?” Then he said: He feeds my food without my ordering him, and he said another time: Without my order. He said: “The reward.” \between you\"""""""
"2301","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Basri al-San’ani reported, saying: Khaled told us, meaning: Ibn al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ibn Abi told me Burdah. He said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Every Muslim must pay charity.” It was said: Have you seen if not He finds her? He said: “He works with his hand, so he benefits himself and gives in charity.” It was said: What do you think if he does not do that? He said: “He helps the one in need who is in need.” It was said: What if he does not do that? He said: “He commands good.” It was said: What do you think if he does not do it? He said: “He refrains from evil, for it is charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2302","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, saying: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, saying: I heard Abu Wael speaking, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If a woman gives alms from her husband’s house, She has a reward, and the husband has the same, and the treasurer has the same, and each of them does not diminish the reward of its owner in the slightest, for the husband. “For what he earned, and she gets the right for what she spent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2303","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Hussein Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that his father He told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he stood up as a preacher, and he said in his sermon: “No.” It is permissible for a woman to give a gift except with her husband’s permission.”, Summary"
"2304","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani reported, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah reported, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Aisha, the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered with him and said: Which of us will catch up with you the fastest? He said: “I have the longest hand among you.” So they took a reed and extended it, and it was black. They quickly caught up with it, and it was the longest hand among them. This was due to the abundance of charity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2305","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: A man said: O Messenger of God, which charity is better? He said: “To give in charity when you are healthy and stingy, hoping for a living, and fearing poverty.”"
"2306","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed al-Qattan told us, he said: Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: I heard Musa bin Talha, that Hakim bin Hizam told him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best charity is that which is given over the back of wealth, and a high hand is better than a low hand.” lower, and start with those you support.”"
"2307","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr narrated, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus narrated, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa`id narrated to me Ibn Al-Musayyab said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best charity is that which is done from the appearance of wealth. “And start with those you support.”"
"2308","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated, saying: Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari narrates, on the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If a man spends on his family while hoping for it… It was charity for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2309","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man from Banu Adhra emancipated a slave of his. Some time later, this reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Do you have anyone else’s wealth?” He said: No, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who? “So Nu’aym bin Abdullah Al-Adawi bought it for eight hundred dirhams, and he brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and paid for it.” To him, then he said: “Start with yourself and give alms to it, and if there is any left over, then to your family, and if anything left over from your family, then to your relatives. If there is anything left over from your relatives, then this and that.” He says: “Before your hands, on your right, and on your left.”"
"2310","Muhammad bin Mansour informed us of the Meccan passport, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, he said: I heard Abu Kitten. Then Abu Al-Zinad told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the example of a spender who gives in charity The miserly person is like two men wearing two garments or two robes of iron from their breasts to their throats. If the spender wants to spend, The shield is widened over him or passed around until its borders are closed and its effect is removed, and if the miserly person wants to spend, it is shortened and each ring sticks to its place. Even if it took him by his collarbone or his neck,” Abu Hurairah says: “I bear witness that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He expands it, but it does not expand. Tawus said: I heard Abu Hurairah gesturing with his hand as he expanded it, but it did not expand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
